.TH PEIPKG 1
.SH NAME
peipkg \- manage packages on a Peios system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B peipkg
.RB [ --root " " ROOT ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGUMENTS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B peipkg
is the live-system Peios package consumer.  It installs, upgrades, removes,
queries, verifies, and recovers packages and manages configured repositories.
.PP
The default operating root is
.BR / .
A literal path or a registered Peios root may be selected with
.BR --root .
.SH COMMANDS
.BR install ,
.BR upgrade ,
.BR downgrade ,
.BR uninstall ,
.BR remove ,
.BR claim ,
.BR undo ,
.BR list ,
.BR info ,
.BR files ,
.BR owns ,
.BR search ,
.BR verify ,
.BR history ,
.BR repo ,
.BR root ,
.BR refresh ,
.BR clean ,
and
.BR recover .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /lcl/conf/peipkg
Repository configuration in the writable backing store.
.TP
.I /var/state/peipkg
Package database, transaction journal, lock, and verified repository cache.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR peipkg-compose (1),
.BR peipkg-repo (1)
